# Canonical authorship. Maps the identities this repository was committed under
# onto one name and address, so `git shortlog`, `git log`, and GitHub's own
# attribution show a single author instead of four.
#
# This changes how history is *displayed*, not history itself — no commit is
# rewritten and no SHA moves. Added when the repository went public, at which
# point the machine-hostname address below would otherwise have been visible on
# every commit that carried it.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> [Commit Name] <commit@email>

Saransh Hardaha <saranshhardaha05@gmail.com> Saransh <saranshhardaha05@gmail.com>
Saransh Hardaha <saranshhardaha05@gmail.com> <saranshh@MAM5.local>
